                "dsDescriptionValue": {
                  "typeName": "dsDescriptionValue",
                  "multiple": false,
                  "typeClass": "primitive",
                  "value": "<p>This is a corpus of 55 reports in pdf published by the OECD Studies on Water between 2009 and 2021.  This is the basis of the project funded by e-Science center and ODISSEI consotrium awarded to ESSB in EUR in 2022.</p>\n<p>The codes produced are availalbe on Github at the following links -- with methodology, samlping and results listed there.</p>\n<p>Structured Topc Modelling (STM) --   </p>\n<p>GitHub link: <a href=\"https://github.com/disaster-capitalism/topic-modelling\" target=\"_blank\">https://https://github.com/disaster-capitalism/topic-modelling</a></p>\n<p>Word frequencies of executive summaries vis a vis main texts --   </p>\n<p>GitHub link: <a href=\"https://github.com/disaster-capitalism/topic-modelling\" target=\"_blank\">https://https://github.com/disaster-capitalism/topic-modelling</a></p>\n<p>Named Entity Recognition and Semantic Label Mapping --  <a href=\"https://github.com/disaster-capitalism/named-entities\" target=\"_blank\">https://github.com/disaster-capitalism/named-entities</a> </p>\n<p><br></p>\n<p>The data is licensed by OECD and can be obtained from OECD by request. The data description is to be found here -- <a href=\"https://www.oecd-ilibrary.org/environment/oecd-studies-on-water_22245081\" target=\"_blank\">https://https://www.oecd-ilibrary.org/environment/oecd-studies-on-water_22245081</a></p>"
                }
              }
